# adjectives (after 'is')
immutable | mutable | deterministic | stateful | empty | full | idempotent | bounded | unbounded | persistent | closed | busy | daemonic | monochrome | true | false
# comparisons (followed by a number or the <type> "<name>"); equality: is, is not
is at least | is greater than | is bounded by | is at most | is less than
# core: mode before the verb, quantifier, copula
does not | never | always | exceptionally | every | is | is not
# declared absences (presupposed role left empty on purpose)
needs no authentication (authentication)
needs no validation (validation)
needs no synchronization (synchronization)
has no limit (limit)
has no seed (seed)
has no unit (unit)
has no tie-breaker (tie-breaker)
has no reference (reference)
has no default (default)
has no initial state (initial state)
